{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And if these three.</b> Her food, her clothing, and her conjugal rights." "<b>[And if these three.</b> One of these three.]" "<b>And she shall go out free.</b> By a court. Here it did not explain to you when; and it explained to you in another place: 'When your brother, the Hebrew, or the Hebrewess, is sold to you, and your slave serves you six years.' 'Without money' — if she fell ill at the end of six and was unable to go out, and he provides her sustenance, she does not pay. Jerusalemite. And according to its plain sense, 'without money' is a redundant expression, like 'you are dead and shall not live.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:17.110633022Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}